      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "When writing shaders, it's already possible to determine the object scale, once way to do so is using the unity_ObjectToWorld matrix. Usually what you want to do is apply vertex offsets in local space before transforming it to world space to retain the offsets relation to the object regardless of the size. A variable like this would also have to be declared for each avatar, not just the local one. Do you see any other benefit to having something like this?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
