  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-08-01T09:05:51.587Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Certain shader features, such as fur length or outline width, are sensitive to the avatar’s world scale and require adjustment when the avatar is scaled. While this can be done with animators, this won’t work when animations are blocked by safety settings, and add additional CPU load and avatar build complexity. It would be useful if vrchat could inject material properties to all meshes on an avatar to expose the current avatar scale.",
